From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 11:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] boot: fdt_support: sun5i AHB/MBUS settle in fdt_fixup_memory_banks

Three read-after-write stalls in fdt_fixup_memory_banks() on sun5i:

1. fdt_find_or_add_subnode() may call fdt_add_subnode() which writes
   the /memory node; fdt_setprop("device_type") then reads that
   newly-written structure -> stall.

2. fdt_setprop("device_type") writes to blob; fdt_pack_reg() reads
   #address-cells from root node -> stall.

3. fdt_pack_reg() reads blob; fdt_setprop("reg") writes again;
   caller's first post-FDT read then stalls.

All three guards use #ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I.

CRITICAL: Use udelay() (TIMER MMIO read) not a raw DRAM busy-wait loop.
The raw loop's own first iteration reads the counter from the stack
(DRAM). If the MBUS write-buffer is still in flight, that read itself
stalls indefinitely — making the settle useless. udelay() reads a
hardware timer MMIO register which does not share the MBUS stall path.

Settle times: 50ms for write -> read on blob, 5ms before write-only.
All guards: #ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
---
--- a/boot/fdt_support.c
+++ b/boot/fdt_support.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <abuf.h>
 #include <env.h>
 #include <log.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <mapmem.h>
 #include <net.h>
 #include <stdio_dev.h>
@@ -483,6 +484,23 @@
 	if (nodeoffset < 0)
 			return nodeoffset;

+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I
+	/*
+	 * sun5i AHB/MBUS: fdt_find_or_add_subnode() may have called
+	 * fdt_add_subnode() which writes the /memory node into the DTB blob.
+	 * fdt_setprop("device_type") next reads that newly-written structure;
+	 * if the AHB write buffer is still in flight the read stalls.
+	 *
+	 * Use udelay() (TIMER MMIO read) not a raw DRAM busy-wait loop:
+	 * the loop's own first iteration reads _s from the stack (DRAM),
+	 * which itself stalls when the MBUS write-buffer is still in flight.
+	 */
+	printf("[FIXUP-DBG] pre device_type settle\n");
+	asm volatile("mcr p15, 0, %0, c7, c10, 4" :: "r"(0) : "memory");
+	udelay(50000);
+	printf("[FIXUP-DBG] device_type setprop\n");
+#endif
+
 	err = fdt_setprop(blob, nodeoffset, "device_type", "memory",
 			sizeof("memory"));
 	if (err < 0) {
@@ -491,6 +509,20 @@
 		return err;
 	}

+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I
+	/*
+	 * sun5i AHB/MBUS: fdt_setprop("device_type") wrote to the DTB blob
+	 * in DRAM.  fdt_pack_reg() below reads #address-cells from the root
+	 * node; if that cache line was evicted the AHB write buffer stalls
+	 * the subsequent DRAM read indefinitely.
+	 * Use udelay() so the timer MMIO read does not itself stall on DRAM.
+	 */
+	printf("[FIXUP-DBG] pre pack_reg settle\n");
+	asm volatile("mcr p15, 0, %0, c7, c10, 4" :: "r"(0) : "memory");
+	udelay(50000);
+	printf("[FIXUP-DBG] pack_reg\n");
+#endif
+
 	for (i = 0; i < banks; i++) {
 		if (start[i] == 0 && size[i] == 0)
 			break;
@@ -503,6 +535,18 @@

 	len = fdt_pack_reg(blob, tmp, start, size, banks);

+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I
+	/*
+	 * sun5i AHB/MBUS: settle before fdt_setprop("reg") writes to the
+	 * blob, to prevent the caller's first post-FDT DRAM read from
+	 * stalling on the residual write burst.
+	 */
+	printf("[FIXUP-DBG] pre reg setprop settle\n");
+	asm volatile("mcr p15, 0, %0, c7, c10, 4" :: "r"(0) : "memory");
+	udelay(5000);
+	printf("[FIXUP-DBG] reg setprop\n");
+#endif
+
 	err = fdt_setprop(blob, nodeoffset, "reg", tmp, len);
 	if (err < 0) {
 		printf("WARNING: could not set %s %s.\n",
